+## Paired local-LAN device resolution candidate
+
+`INTEGRATION-FIX-011T-B` adds one non-mutating bootstrap route under protocol/schema `1 / 1`:
+
+```text
+POST /devices/resolve
+```
+
+The request requires JSON, a valid canonical `x-swrlz-pairing-token`, and a
+valid `x-swrlz-request-id`. The caller must be loopback or an approved IPv4
+local-LAN peer on the same interface prefix. Existing group, registration,
+join, and check-in mutations remain loopback-only.
+
+Unknown device identities may resolve to `UNKNOWN` without creating records.
+Known active devices require a Keystore-protected proof binding. Pre-contract
+known devices with no sidecar binding return:
+
+```text
+ACTION_REQUIRED / PROOF_ENROLLMENT_REQUIRED
+```
+
+A bound device signs the exact request body and canonical request fields using
+a SERVER- and device-specific HKDF-SHA256 proof key. Timestamp, nonce,
+request-ID, and replay checks fail closed. Resolution never creates or updates
+a device, membership, group, session, trust, administrator, mission, or Truth
+Firewall record.
